OL,3,GNEWSAReduced rail service continues due
OL,4,Ato dry weather
OL,5,
OL,6,FA rail operator has confirmed its
OL,7,Freduced timetable will remain in place
OL,8,Fbecause of the dry weather.
OL,10,FSouth Western Railway (SWR) said the
OL,11,Fservice between Exeter St Davids and
OL,12,FLondon Waterloo would remain two-hourly
OL,13,Fand speed restrictions would continue
OL,14,Funtil there was "significant rainfall".
OL,16,FThe Salisbury to Exeter Rail User Group
OL,17,F(SERUG) has described the early morning
OL,18,Ftimetable as "unacceptable" for
OL,19,Fcommuters in east Devon.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
